{"is_source_file": true, "format": "C", "description": "This file implements the mod_progress plugin for the lighttpd server. It tracks connection progress using unique identifiers, manages tasks related to connection monitoring, handles plugin initialization and cleanup, and provides API functions for tracking and displaying progress status. It defines data structures for nodes, worker data, jobs, and parameters, and includes logic for handling HTTP requests to show progress status in different formats.", "external_files": ["<lighttpd/base.h>", "<lighttpd/lighttpd-glue.h>"], "external_methods": ["li_plugin_register", "li_plugin_free", "li_waitqueue_init", "li_waitqueue_push", "li_waitqueue_pop", "li_waitqueue_update", "li_waitqueue_remove", "li_vrequest_handle_direct", "li_chunkqueue_append_string", "li_vrequest_joblist_append", "li_collect_start", "li_collect_break", "li_http_header_overwrite", "li_vrequest_is_handled", "li_value_get_single_argument", "li_value_type", "li_value_type_string", "li_value_wrap_in_list", "li_handler_new_function", "li_http_method_from_string"], "published": ["mod_progress_init", "mod_progress_free"], "classes": [{"name": "mod_progress_node", "description": "Represents a tracked connection state with identifier, associated request, sizes, and status."}, {"name": "mod_progress_data", "description": "Holds plugin-wide data, including plugin pointer, TTL, and worker-specific data."}, {"name": "mod_progress_worker_data", "description": "Per-worker data including hash table for tracking nodes and timeout queue."}, {"name": "mod_progress_show_param", "description": "Parameters for progress show response, including format and plugin reference."}, {"name": "mod_progress_job", "description": "Job context for collecting and presenting progress data for a particular request."}], "methods": [{"name": "void progress_timeout_callback(liWaitQueue * wq,gpointer data)", "description": "Handles timeout events for the progress tracking wait queue, removin